{title: Wayfaring Stranger}
{artist: Traditional American}
{key: Am}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 3/4}
{difficulty: intermediate}
{tags: folk, spiritual}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [Am]am a poor wayfaring stranger
[Dm]Traveling [Am]through this world of woe
Yet there's no sickness, toil nor danger
In that bright [E]world to which I [Am]go
I'm [F]going there to see my [C]father
I'm [F]going there no more to [E]roam
I'm [Am]only going over Jordan
I'm only [E]going over [Am]home

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [Am]know dark clouds will gather 'round me
[Dm]I know my [Am]way is rough and steep
Yet beauteous fields lie just before me
Where God's re[E]deemed their vigils [Am]keep
I'm [F]going there to see my [C]mother
She [F]said she'd meet me when I [E]come
I'm [Am]only going over Jordan
I'm only [E]going over [Am]home
